+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent is configured with toolChoice 'required', which forces the model to make a tool call on every turn, so after the supervisor declines approveRefund it cannot write a final text reply and instead keeps calling tools (approveRefund again, lookupOrder) until maxTurns is exhausted.",
+  "evidence": "Reproduced with the real model: on the original code, sending the refund request, then declining the approveRefund interrupt with {approved: false, note: 'duplicate claim'}, produces a second approveRefund interrupt and then fails with AgentError 'ABORTED: Exceeded maximum tool call iterations (6)'. With toolChoice changed to 'auto', the same sequence finishes with finishReason 'stop', no pending interrupts, and the reply 'I'm sorry, your refund for order A-1001 was not approved because it appears to be a duplicate claim.'"
+}
